@*
    Real-data read-only environment notice.

    This is not an error and must not be styled as one. The environment is working exactly as
    configured: real Turuncu Hat and Jira data can be read, and every external write is fenced off.
    An operator who reads this as a fault will go looking for an outage that does not exist.

    It is also deliberately distinct from the simulation banner. Simulation means the data itself is
    synthetic. This means the data is real — which is the more consequential state, because what is
    on screen is genuine operational information even though nothing can be written back.

    Neutral container with a single brand accent rule, not a red alert surface.
*@

@if (Active)
{
    <div class="so-readonly" role="status">
        <span class="so-readonly-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.EditOff" />
        </span>
        <div class="so-readonly-text">
            <p class="so-readonly-title">GERÇEK VERİ — YAZMA KAPALI</p>
            <p class="so-readonly-body">@Explanation</p>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>Backend-supplied fallback used when no server notice is returned.</summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Says what still works before what does not. The operator's first question in this mode is
    /// "can I trust what I am looking at", and the answer is yes.
    /// </remarks>
    public const string DefaultNotice =
        "Gerçek Turuncu Hat ve Jira verileri okunabilir. Jira kaydı oluşturma ve kaynak kayıt "
        + "güncelleme işlemleri bu TEST modunda kapalıdır.";

    /// <summary>Whether the backend reported <c>readOnlyIntegrationMode</c> for this response.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Active { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Server-supplied <c>readOnlyNotice</c>, when one was returned.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Notice { get; set; }

    // The server's wording wins when present; the constant is a fallback, not a default the UI
    // asserts over the backend.
    private string Explanation =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Notice) ? DefaultNotice : Notice!;
}
